  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Given that&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>45</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math>&nbsp;of the acid of molecular mass&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>90</mn></math>&nbsp;was neutralized by&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>20</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>ml</mi></math>&nbsp;of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></mfenced></math>&nbsp;caustic potash.</p><p>We know that,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Normality</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>Weight</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>of</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>the</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>base</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>1000</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>Eq</mi><mo>.</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>weight</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><mi>volume</mi></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8757;</mo></math> Gram equivalents of an acid</p><p>Gram equivalents of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>KOH</mi></math> i.e. <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>45</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>20</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><mn>1000</mn></mfrac></math></p><p>where, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mo>=</mo></math> Equivalent mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>45</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>1000</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>20</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>45</mn></math></p><p>Thus, basicity <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>90</mn><mn>45</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math>&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mo>&#8757;</mo><mi>Basicity</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>Molecular</mi><mo>mass</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>Equivalent</mi><mo>mass</mo></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math></p>",
